# ucrom touch-only kernel fragment (applied to every SoC, both flavors).
# Keyboards and mice never get a driver; no keyboard-driven kernel features.
#
# CONFIG_VT stays enabled on purpose: the Phosh session is a logind session
# on a virtual terminal (tty7) and Halium requires it. A VT without any
# usable keyboard is not an input path: no getty runs on any VT, SysRq is off
# and every keyboard is inhibited in the kernel before anything can read it.
# CONFIG_USB_HID is not set
# CONFIG_USB_HIDDEV is not set
# CONFIG_USB_KBD is not set
# CONFIG_USB_MOUSE is not set
# CONFIG_BT_HIDP is not set
# CONFIG_UHID is not set
# CONFIG_USB_CONFIGFS_F_HID is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT_MOUSEDEV is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT_KEYBOARD_USB is not set
# CONFIG_MAGIC_SYSRQ is not set
